From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:52:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libutils: Thread::run takes the first strong reference for
 vendor code

Since Android 12 run() uses sp<Thread>::fromExisting(this), which aborts
when the Thread is not owned by an sp<> yet. Legacy vendor blobs create
threads with a raw new and run them immediately: the Nougat MediaTek camera
HAL on the Meizu MX6 (P2Procedure::createProcessor, libmtkcam_hwnode.so)
aborted the camera provider with 'incStrongRequireStrong() called on ...
which isn't already owned' on every configureStreams, so the camera opened
without a preview. In the VNDK variant, take the reference as run() did
before (force_set); the system variant keeps the strict check.

Change-Id: I1f56f9f9e94d21cd523a7d18179c57e0b6fdf2be

diff --git a/libutils/Threads.cpp b/libutils/Threads.cpp
index e756fec..f1e34e2 100644
--- a/libutils/Threads.cpp
+++ b/libutils/Threads.cpp
@@ -673,7 +673,19 @@ status_t Thread::run(const char* name, int32_t priority, size_t stack)
     mThread = thread_id_t(-1);
 
     // hold a strong reference on ourself
+#if defined(__ANDROID_VNDK__)
+    // Legacy vendor code creates a Thread with a raw new and calls run() before
+    // any sp<> owns it (Meizu MX6: the Nougat MediaTek camera HAL,
+    // P2Procedure::createProcessor in libmtkcam_hwnode.so), which fromExisting()
+    // turns into "incStrongRequireStrong() called on ... which isn't already
+    // owned" and an abort of the camera provider. The vendor (VNDK) variant takes
+    // the reference the way run() did before Android 12; the system variant keeps
+    // the strict check.
+    mHoldSelf.clear();
+    mHoldSelf.force_set(this);
+#else
     mHoldSelf = sp<Thread>::fromExisting(this);
+#endif
 
     mRunning = true;
 
